From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 18:26:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] h2: client: the sid 1 headers-first rule asks the sid 1 child

A client stream other than sid 1 is held back until sid 1 has sent its
headers.  The rule tested the parser's current-stream pointer, which
between frames on stream 0 (eg, a PING) is the connection wsi itself, and
the connection stays in LRS_H2_WAITING_TO_SEND_HEADERS for its whole life:
after a server PING every later request on a pooled connection waited
until it timed out.  Google's front ends send a PING right after each
response, so every second fetch to them failed.

Ask the sid 1 child instead.

Backport of the rops_perform_user_POLLOUT_h2() hunk of upstream
a18023d26d649951c26dab5c099345721de1f15b (main, "h2: a client connection
whose request moved to sid 1 is established, not a flag"), adapted to
v5.0-stable ac23cae70: client_mux_migrated instead of
lws_wsi_client_nwsi_migrated(); the rest of that commit (the connection
state rework) is not carried.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
  lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c |   22 ++++++++++++++++++----
  1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c b/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c
--- a/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c
+++ b/lib/roles/h2/ops-h2.c
@@ -1284,10 +1284,24 @@ rops_perform_user_POLLOUT_h2(struct lws *wsi)
 
 #if defined(LWS_WITH_CLIENT)
 		if (lwsi_state(w) == LRS_H2_WAITING_TO_SEND_HEADERS) {
-			if (w->mux.my_sid != 1 && (!wsi->client_mux_migrated ||
-			    (wsi->h2.h2n->swsi && lwsi_state(wsi->h2.h2n->swsi) == LRS_H2_WAITING_TO_SEND_HEADERS))) {
-				lwsl_info("%s: waiting for sid 1 to send headers\n", __func__);
-				continue;
+			if (w->mux.my_sid != 1) {
+				/*
+				 * Ask the sid 1 child itself: the parser's
+				 * current-stream pointer is the connection wsi
+				 * between frames on stream 0 (eg, a PING), and
+				 * the connection sits in WAITING_TO_SEND_HEADERS
+				 * for its whole life, so testing it stalls every
+				 * later stream until it times out
+				 */
+				struct lws *s1 = lws_wsi_mux_from_id(wsi, 1);
+
+				if (!wsi->client_mux_migrated ||
+				    (s1 && lwsi_state(s1) ==
+						LRS_H2_WAITING_TO_SEND_HEADERS)) {
+					lwsl_info("%s: waiting for sid 1 to send headers\n",
+						  __func__);
+					continue;
+				}
 			}
 
 			if (lws_h2_client_handshake(w))
